{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#117","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#117","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#117\",\"parent_revision\":\"ef631345e77371705125eea6437eed533d0ab6e4cda90130b5c845d47e392997\",\"root_revision\":\"ef631345e77371705125eea6437eed533d0ab6e4cda90130b5c845d47e392997\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`skilllint check --fix` rewrites files and prints nothing about what it touched. A user who runs it sees exit 0 and an unchanged-looking terminal, then discovers the edits in `git diff` \u2014 or does not.\\n\\nTwo mechanics make this worse:\\n\\n- `--fix` invokes every validator's `can_fix()` regardless of whether that validator reported an issue, so writers run against files nothing flagged.\\n- Fix results are collected and then discarded rather than summarised.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nGate `fix()` on the validator having actually reported a fixable issue, and print the collected fix summaries \u2014 which file, which rule, what changed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #114 \u2014 the PL006 marketplace writer, the concrete data-loss instance this silence hid\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1ffefd0dbee92c9547606a167f8e37b5f1b7c24d0577eb9cf9d1a383e780cf7f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-LVg\"}"}